  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason (skewness) is not considered by the individual. The individual does not discuss the distribution of losses, the probability of large losses, or any feature of the tail structure. Instead, they focus solely on expected losses. The decision reason prefers the more right-skewed lottery — which, as calculated, is A (due to a 20% chance of a larger loss of -4000), not B. The individual’s justification (choosing B due to lower expected loss) is inconsistent with the rule of the decision reason. Therefore, the individual did not use the skewness-based reason to make the decision. The reported reasoning is based on expected value, not skewness.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
